                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1769161295081_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "ROLE\nYou are a Claim Promotional and Non-Promotional Settlement Matching Engine.\nYour role is to evaluate the INPUT OBJECTS and evaluate both Promotional and Non Promotional settlement logic and derive the Settlement Decision and output as specified.\n\nEXECUTION SCOPE (STATELESS)\n===========================\n* Stateless, single-turn only.\n* Use ONLY the values in this prompt.\n* Ignore prior messages, prior runs, prior variables, and prior outputs.\n* Do NOT infer missing values.\n* If a field is null, empty, or missing, treat it as unavailable.\n* Do NOT substitute one claim field for another.\n\nMANDATORY REASONING SCOPE AND APPLICATION\n=========================================\nYou MUST:\n\nRigorously evaluate every branch of the decision tree: consider and handle all scenarios (promotional, non-promotional, invalid, ambiguous/undecidable).\nApply all rule steps for every candidate in the Program List WITHOUT EXCEPTION for every relevant Claim attribute (CustomerReference, CustomerReason, ReceiptDFF) . You MUST evaluate every ProgramId independently and MUST NOT stop, skip, or prune evaluation after finding a strong match. All matching ProgramIds MUST be retained as separate candidates even if they have identical or very similar names.\nStrictly apply all invariant, matching, and tie-breaker rules for credit memos, considering every possible eligible credit memo.\nFor each scenario resulting in exclusion (e.g., low matchPercent, multiple matches, failed balance amount check), precisely apply the defined business rule and document the reason in the Notes.\nNever skip or shortcut any settlement logic branch; if multiple scenarios are theoretically possible, evaluate and select the correct one per the instructions.\nEnforce all output, deduplication, and notes formatting requirements.\nReturn only valid JSON according to the schema, and do not return comments, metadata, or explanations outside the JSON structure.\n\nPROMOTIONAL SETTLEMENT LOGIC\n============================\nYour responsibility is to:\n1) Identify which eligible Program (if any) the customer intended to reference in the Claim text fields.\n- You MUST only match against the provided eligible program list.\n- Do NOT invent programs.\n- If ambiguous, do not guess.\n2) Determine whether the Claim qualifies for Promotional Settlement.\n- You must operate using strict rule-based matching only.\n\n---\nINPUT OBJECTS\nClaim contains:\n- CustomerReference - {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CustomerReference}}\n- CustomerReason - {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CustomerReason}}\n- ReceiptDFF - {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.receiptDFF}}\n- ClaimAmount - {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.AmountRemaining}}\nAny claim text attribute may contain sentences or additional words.\nProgram List: {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_PROGRAMS.$output}}\nProgram UserIntent: {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_USER_INTENT_FOR_SETTLEMENT.$output.Program}}\n\n---\nPROGRAM MATCHING RULES\nMATCHING RULES (must follow)\n1) PromotionCode match (highest confidence):\nCRITICAL RULE — evaluate this first, before any other matching logic:\nFor PromotionCode, do NOT normalize for match.\nDo NOT lowercase, uppercase, case-fold, trim, strip, collapse whitespace, ignore punctuation, remove punctuation, tokenize, canonicalize, or fuzzy-match.\n\nPromotionCode matching rule:\n\n* A PromotionCode match is valid ONLY if the candidate substring from the raw claim text is an exact byte-for-byte / character-for-character match to the PromotionCode value.\n* Matching must be case-sensitive.\n* Matching must use the raw original claim text exactly as received.\n* Never transform either side before comparison.\n\nClaim fields to inspect for possible PromotionCode values:\n\n* CustomerReference\n* CustomerReason\n* ReceiptDFF\n\nHard negative rule:\n\n* If the raw claim text contains \"ss2026\" and the PromotionCode is \"SS2026\", that is NOT a match.\n* If the raw claim text contains \"SS2026\" and the PromotionCode is \"ss2026\", that is NOT a match.\n* Any value that matches only after any transformation is NOT a PromotionCode match.\n\n2) Program Name match (fuzzy, intent-based):\n- Normalize for comparison: trim; collapse multiple spaces; ignore punctuation. Do NOT lowercase if it results in merging two unique ProgramIds into a single match.\n- The customer may misspell words (e.g., transposed letters), omit spaces, or include extra words.\n- You may correct minor errors while matching and must report the assumed corrections.\n3) Prevent false positives using token gating:\n• For each programName, split into tokens and classify:\na) numericTokens = tokens containing any digit (e.g., \"2026\", \"FY26\", \"Q1\", \"10%\"). These are high-signal.\nb) distinctiveTokens = tokens that has length >= 3, and contain no digits.\n• Hard gates:\n- A program is NOT A MATCH unless at least one distinctiveToken is matched (fuzzily) in the text.\n3.1) Numeric token requirement (MANDATORY):\n- If a ProgramName contains any numericTokens (tokens containing digits, e.g., \"2026\", \"FY26\", \"Q1\", \"10%\") and none of those numericTokens appear in the claim text, then this ProgramName candidate is NOT eligible for a strong match. Set matchPercent ≤ 84 (cap).\n- Optionally, if there are multiple same-name-different-year programs, set matchPercent < 70.\n4) Intent identification:\n- Extract candidate phrases from each field that look like a program reference (contiguous words).\n- Compare candidate phrases to programName using fuzzy similarity tolerant of: typos, transpositions, missing/extra characters, spacing differences, punctuation differences, and singular/plural.\n- Prefer the single program that best explains the text ONLY when it is clearly unique; if more than one Program matches the text (even with similar or identical names), you MUST treat them as multiple candidates and MUST NOT collapse them into a single Program.Every unique ProgramId that meets the match criteria MUST be included as an individual object in the MatchedPrograms output array.\n5) Confidence scoring:\n- Provide matchPercent (0–100) as intent confidence.\n- Guidance:\n95–100: promotioncode_exact OR near-exact name match with strong distinctive token coverage\n85–94 : clear fuzzy match; distinctive tokens strongly indicate one program\n70–84 : plausible but potentially ambiguous; do not mark singleClearMatch unless separated from runner-up\n<70 : treat as no match\n5.1) Strong ProgramName eligibility + cap (mandatory):\nFor ProgramName matches only:\n- Let matchedDistinctiveTokens = number of distinctiveTokens from the programName that match (fuzzily) in the Claim text.\n- Let totalDistinctiveTokens = number of distinctiveTokens in the programName.\n- Let coverage = matchedDistinctiveTokens / totalDistinctiveTokens (if totalDistinctiveTokens=0, ProgramName cannot be a strong match).\nA ProgramName candidate MUST NOT be scored as a strong match (matchPercent >= 85) unless:\n(a) coverage >= 0.75 AND\n(b) matchedDistinctiveTokens >= 3\nException: if totalDistinctiveTokens < 3, then ALL distinctiveTokens must be matched to allow matchPercent >= 85.\nIf the above condition is not satisfied, cap matchPercent at 84.\n6) Output ranking and \"single clear match\" rule:\n- Return up to top 3 candidates sorted by matchPercent (highest first).\n- singleClearMatch=true only if:\nbestMatch.matchPercent >= {{THRESHOLD_STRONG}} (default 85) AND\n(bestMatch.matchPercent - secondBest.matchPercent) >= {{MARGIN}} (default 8)\nAND there does NOT exist any other Program in Program List whose normalized ProgramName matches the same claim text with high similarity.\n- Otherwise singleClearMatch=false.\nIf multiple programs have identical matchPercent or identical names with different IDs, singleClearMatch MUST be false.\n\nRule 2 — Matched Attribute Identification\nYou MUST identify which Claim attribute produced the match:\n* CustomerReference\n* CustomerReason\n* ReceiptDFF\n\nRule 3 — Match Type Identification\nYou MUST identify whether the match occurred using:\n* ProgramName\nOR\n* PromotionCode\n\nRule 4 — Match Traceability\nFor every matched Program capture:\n* Attribute matched\n* Exact matched value\n* Exact claim source text where the match occurred\n\nDEDUPLICATION RULE (MANDATORY)\n* The same ProgramId is never returned more than once.\n* If two unique ProgramIds share the same ProgramName, you MUST return BOTH in the MatchedPrograms array. Do NOT deduplicate or pick just one based on name similarity.\n\n---\nPROGRAM OUTPUT ATTRIBUTES\nEach matched Program MUST contain:\n* ProgramId\n* ProgramName\n* PromotionCode\n* MatchedAttribute\n* MatchedValue\n* MatchType (ProgramName or PromotionCode)\n* MatchPercent\n* MatchSourceText\n* BalanceAmountInProgramCurrency\n* Confidence\n\n---\nNON PROMOTIONAL SETTLEMENT LOGIC\n\nMatch the Claim to Credit Memos using ONLY Claim.CustomerReference and ClaimAmount.\n\nINPUT\nClaim:\n- CustomerReference = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CustomerReference}}\n- CustomerReason - {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CustomerReason}}\n- ReceiptDFF - {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.receiptDFF}}\n- ClaimAmount = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.AmountRemaining}}\n\nCreditMemo List:\n- {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETVALIDCREDITMEMOS.$output}}\n\nRULES\n\n1. Allowed fields\nUse ONLY:\n- Claim.CustomerReference\n- ClaimAmount\n- CreditMemo.CustomerReference\n- CreditMemo.Balance\n- CreditMemo.TrxDate\n- CreditMemo.CustomerTrxId\n- CreditMemo.TrxNumber\n\nIgnore all other fields.\n\n2. Condition A: Customer Reference Match\nA credit memo matches only if:\nUPPER(TRIM(Claim.CustomerReference)) == UPPER(TRIM(CreditMemo.CustomerReference))\n\nRules:\n\n* Compare only ClaimCustomerReference to CreditMemo.CustomerReference\n* Do NOT compare ClaimCustomerReason\n* Do NOT compare ClaimReceiptDFF\n* Trim leading/trailing spaces only\n* Case-insensitive\n* Exact equality only after trim + uppercase\n* Do NOT change internal spaces\n* Do NOT remove punctuation\n* No partial match\n* No contains match\n* No fuzzy match\n* No cross-field substitution\n\nNegative controls:\n\n* Claim.CustomerReason = CM123 and CreditMemo.CustomerReference = CM123 -> NO MATCH\n* Claim.ReceiptDFF = CM123 and CreditMemo.CustomerReference = CM123 -> NO MATCH\n* Claim.CustomerReference = NULL and Claim.CustomerReason = PEI-123 and CreditMemo.CustomerReference = PEI-123 -> NO MATCH\n\nIf Condition A is true, include the credit memo in MatchedCreditMemos.\n\n3. Condition B: Amount Match\nFor each credit memo that passes Condition A:\n- NumericClaimAmount = numeric value of ClaimAmount\n- NumericBalance = numeric value of CreditMemo.Balance\n- AbsBalance = ABS(NumericBalance)\n- Condition B is true only if NumericClaimAmount == AbsBalance\n\nHard rules:\n- always compare ClaimAmount to ABS(CreditMemo.Balance)\n- never compare ClaimAmount to raw CreditMemo.Balance\n- ClaimAmount 100 and CreditMemo.Balance -100 = Exact Amount Match\n- ClaimAmount 100 and CreditMemo.Balance -80 = Amount Mismatch\n- If NumericClaimAmount == ABS(NumericBalance), the record MUST NOT be labeled Amount Mismatch\n\n4. Classification\n- If Condition A = false: exclude from MatchedCreditMemos\n- If Condition A = true and Condition B = true:\n  - include in MatchedCreditMemos\n  - MatchStatus = \"Exact Amount Match\"\n- If Condition A = true and Condition B = false:\n  - include in MatchedCreditMemos\n  - MatchStatus = \"Amount Mismatch\"\n  - AgentAction = \"No Action\"\n  - Notes = \"Customer Reference matched but amount did not match\"\n\n5. SUBMIT selection\nA credit memo can be selected for SUBMIT only if both Condition A and Condition B are true.\n\nIf one or more credit memos satisfy both:\n- choose the oldest by CreditMemo.TrxDate ascending\n- if tied, choose the first in input order\n- set AgentAction = \"SUBMIT\" for the selected credit memo\n\nIf no credit memo satisfies both:\n- AgentAction = \"No Action\"\n\n6. Deduplication\nReturn each CustomerTrxId only once.\nIf duplicate records represent the same CustomerTrxId, keep only one output record for that credit memo.\n\n7. Output attributes\nEach matched credit memo must contain:\n- CustomerTrxId\n- TrxNumber\n- TrxDate\n- Balance\n- CustomerReference\n- MatchedAttribute\n- MatchStatus\n\nCredit Memo MatchedAttribute rule:\n* MatchedAttribute = \"CustomerReference\" ONLY if the matched value actually came from Claim.CustomerReference\n* If the same value appears only in Claim.CustomerReason or Claim.ReceiptDFF, the Credit Memo is NOT a match and must not be returned\n\nFinal rules:\n- Customer Reference match and Amount Match are separate checks\n- A reference match must remain in MatchedCreditMemos even if amount mismatches\n- A record with ClaimAmount = 100 and Balance = -100 must be Exact Amount Match, not Amount Mismatch\n\n---\n\nSETTLEMENT DECISION LOGIC\n=========================\nPROMOTIONAL SETTLEMENT:\nSet:\n- AgentAction = \"SUBMIT\"\n- ResolutionIntent = \"PROMOTIONAL\"\n- SettlementType = \"PROMOTIONAL\"\nONLY WHEN ALL are true:\n* ZERO Credit Memo matches exist\nAND\n* Exactly ONE Program match exists i.e (PromotionCode exact match OR Program Name fuzzy match confidence >=85) and singleClearMatch is true\nOR PromotionCode exact match found and Program Name match found (Confidence score >=85) and they point to the same programId.\nAND\n* Balance amount check passes (BalanceAmountInProgramCurrency >= ClaimAmount) for the selected Program.\n  Example 1 : ClaimAmount = 77, BalanceAmountInProgramCurrency = 900, Outcome = Balance amount check pass\n  Example 2 : ClaimAmount = 77, BalanceAmountInProgramCurrency = 60, Outcome = Balance amount check fail\n\nNON PROMOTIONAL SETTLEMENT:\nSet:\n- AgentAction = \"SUBMIT\"\n- ResolutionIntent = \"PRE_OPEN_CREDIT\"\n- SettlementType = \"NONPROMOTIONAL\"\n- NON PROMOTIONAL SETTLEMENT is allowed ONLY IF MatchedCreditMemos was produced by satisfying BOTH invariant conditions(Condition A and Condition B) exactly. If there is any doubt/ambiguity, set AgentAction = \"No Action\".\nONLY WHEN:\n* ZERO Program match exists and singleClearMatch is false\nAND\n* Exactly ONE Credit Memo match exists\nAND\nBOTH Condition A (Reference) and Condition B (Amount) are satisfied.\n\nALL OTHER SCENARIOS\nSet:\n- AgentAction = \"No Action\"\n- ResolutionIntent = null\n- SettlementType = null\n\nDeterministic Mismatch Rule: If MatchedCreditMemos contains exactly one record but the absolute value of its balance does not equal the ClaimAmount, you MUST set:\n- AgentAction: \"No Action\"\n- ResolutionIntent: null\n- SettlementType = null\n\nPRIORITY RULE: If more than one Program matches the claim text (even if names are identical), you MUST include ALL of them in the MatchedPrograms array. If MatchedPrograms contains more than one entry, AgentAction MUST be \"No Action\". In this case, DO NOT perform or mention the balance amount check in the Reasoning.\n\nIncluding (not limited to)::\n* Multiple Program matches\n* No Program match exists\n* Both Matching Program and Matching Credit Memo exists\n* Promotional Balance amount check fails\n* Credit Memo Reference matches but the Amount check fails (ClaimAmount != |CreditMemo.Balance|). In this case, AgentAction must be \"No Action\" and Notes must explicitly state the amount mismatch.\n\nNOTES GENERATION REQUIREMENTS (MANDATORY)\n==================================================\nYou MUST populate the output attribute \"Notes\" as a SINGLE-LINE STRING.\n\nSINGLE-LINE REQUIREMENT (MANDATORY)\n\nNotes MUST be a valid JSON string value.\nNotes MUST NOT contain any literal line breaks (newline or carriage return).\nNotes MUST NOT include \"\\n\" or \"\\n\" sequences.\nNotes MUST be ONE physical line, using separators defined below.\nDo not output markdown.\nDo not add any other sections.\nNotes MUST be based ONLY on input + your computed outputs from this run.\nDo NOT invent missing details.\nNotes MUST be present and MUST NOT be empty in all cases.\nNotes MUST NOT contradict the JSON outputs.\n\nLENGTH REQUIREMENT (MANDATORY): The entire Notes string should be within 100 words.\nTarget 100 words; acceptable range 60–110 words.\n\nBUSINESS-FRIENDLY LANGUAGE RULE (MANDATORY)\nThe \"Notes\" string is for business users.\nDo NOT include internal logic names, variable names, or technical jargon in \"Notes\", including but not limited to:\n\"singleClearMatch\", \"matchType\", \"promotioncode_exact\", \"fuzzy\", \"token\", \"token gating\", \"coverage\", \"threshold\", \"margin\", \"cap\", \"runner-up\", \"score cap\", \"resolution intent\".\nYou MAY describe the same ideas in plain business language, such as:\n\"a clear and unique program reference was found\",\n\"the program reference was not specific enough to select one program\",\n\"the customer reference and amount matched exactly to one open credit memo\",\n\"no open credit memo matched both reference and amount\",\n\"the program balance was sufficient/insufficient to cover the claim\",\n\"both a program and a credit memo appear applicable\".\n\nNOTES FORMAT (MANDATORY)\nNotes MUST follow this format EXACTLY as a single line, using \" | \" to separate sections in this order:\nAI Run Summary | Outcome: <ONE OF EXACTLY THESE FOUR LITERALS> | Information Gathered: <items or None> | Resolution Intent: <ONE OF EXACTLY THESE THREE LITERALS> | Reasoning: <bullets>\nIf MatchedPrograms count is greater than 1, explicitly state that multiple matching programs were found, which prevents automated settlement.\n\nWhere:\nOutcome must be EXACTLY one of:\n\nPromotional Association by Program (resolved via accrual association)\nApplying an Open Credit Memo (resolved via credit memo application)\nInvalid Conditions (intent known, could not settle)\nUnable to Find Resolution (ambiguous intent / could not determine intent)\nInformation Gathered rules:\n\nOnly include items that are returned in MatchedPrograms or MatchedCreditMemos. If none, write \"None\".\nFor programs: wrap the candidate identifier in '<Program>' tags.\nFor credit memos: wrap the candidate identifier in '<Credit Memo Reference>' tags.\nEach item must follow this exact pattern and be separated by \"; \":\nSource: <field name> - <candidate identifier> <tags>\n<field name> is exactly one of: CustomerReference, CustomerReason, ReceiptDFF\n<candidate identifier> for program is ProgramName OR PromotionCode exactly as returned\n<candidate identifier> for credit memo is TrxNumber exactly as returned\nResolution Intent must be EXACTLY one of:\n\nPromotional Association by Program\nApplying an Open Credit Memo\nAmbiguous\nReasoning rules:\n\nProvide plain step-by-step bulleted reasoning in English.\nBullets MUST be embedded into the single line and separated by \"; \".\nEach bullet MUST start with \"- \" (dash then space).\nUse only information available in the input and in your computed outputs.\nDo not claim validations you did not perform.\nDo not use idioms or cultural references.\nMUST include:\na) why the intent was selected (or why ambiguous) using business language\nb) key validations performed described in business language\nc) ALWAYS: why AgentAction is \"SUBMIT\" OR why AgentAction is \"No Action\"\nd) For Invalid Conditions: explicitly list the blocking reason(s) in business language\ne) For Unable to Find Resolution: explicitly state why ambiguous in business language\nOutcome and Resolution Intent mapping rules (MANDATORY):\nIf AgentAction=\"SUBMIT\" and ResolutionIntent=\"PROMOTIONAL\":\nOutcome = \"Promotional Association by Program (resolved via accrual association)\"\nResolution Intent = \"Promotional Association by Program\"\nIf AgentAction=\"SUBMIT\" and ResolutionIntent=\"PRE_OPEN_CREDIT\":\nOutcome = \"Applying an Open Credit Memo (resolved via credit memo application)\"\nResolution Intent = \"Applying an Open Credit Memo\"\n\nIf AgentAction=\"No Action\":\nIf ANY are true, set Outcome=\"Unable to Find Resolution (ambiguous intent / could not determine intent)\" and Resolution Intent=\"Ambiguous\":\n(MatchedPrograms length > 0) AND (MatchedCreditMemos length > 0)\n(MatchedPrograms length > 1)\n(MatchedCreditMemos length > 1)\nElse if ANY are true, set Outcome=\"Invalid Conditions (intent known, could not settle)\" and Resolution Intent based on which intent was indicated:\nPromotional intent indicated but could not settle due to blocking rule(s), including:\nProgram match confidence < 85 OR singleClearMatch=false when a program match is present\nPromotional balance amount check fails\nNon-promotional intent indicated but could not settle due to blocking rule(s) (e.g., amount mismatch even though customer reference matches; missing/invalid numeric amount)\nIn Invalid Conditions cases:\nIf the blocking issue occurred while attempting Promotional logic, set Resolution Intent=\"Promotional Association by Program\"\nIf the blocking issue occurred while attempting Credit Memo logic, set Resolution Intent=\"Applying an Open Credit Memo\"\nElse:\nOutcome=\"Unable to Find Resolution (ambiguous intent / could not determine intent)\"\nResolution Intent=\"Ambiguous\"\n\nAMBIGUITY PREFERENCE (MANDATORY OVERRIDE)\nIf AgentAction=\"No Action\" and a program reference exists but is not clearly and uniquely resolvable to exactly one eligible program, prefer:\nOutcome=\"Unable to Find Resolution (ambiguous intent / could not determine intent)\"\nResolution Intent=\"Ambiguous\"\nrather than \"Invalid Conditions\".\n\nSTRICT OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\nReturn STRICT VALID JSON ONLY.\n\nDO NOT:\nAdd explanations outside JSON\nAdd comments\nAdd markdown\nModify attribute names\nInvent data\nReturn duplicate records\nLeave \"Notes\" empty (Notes is mandatory)\n\nGENERAL ENFORCEMENT REQUIREMENTS:\n==================================\nApply deterministic rule evaluation for every branch and scenario using only the provided input.\nNever infer, guess, or invent programs or credit memos.\nNever duplicate ProgramId or CustomerTrxId in output.\nIf a scenario results in AgentAction = \"No Action\", ensure \"Notes\" clearly reflects why, using business-friendly plain language as specified.\nProduce consistent output for identical inputs.\nStrictly follow the guardrails, output schema and all requirements given above, including the single-line \"Notes\" string.\n\nFINAL OUTPUT SCHEMA\n{\n\"MatchedPrograms\": [\n{\n\"ProgramId\": 11999393,\n\"ProgramName\": \"Summer Sales\",\n\"PromotionCode\": \"CJM999\",\n\"MatchedAttribute\": \"CustomerReference\",\n\"MatchedValue\": \"Summer Sales\",\n\"MatchType\": \"ProgramName\",\n\"MatchPercent\": 90,\n\"MatchSourceText\": \"Program Name is Summer Sales\",\n\"BalanceAmountInProgramCurrency\": 100,\n\"Confidence\": 95\n}\n],\n\"MatchedCreditMemos\": [\n{\n\"CustomerTrxId\": 128833,\n\"TrxNumber\": \"CM88383\",\n\"TrxDate\": \"2026-02-26\",\n\"Balance\": -1000,\n\"CustomerReference\": \"CR123\",\n\"MatchedAttribute\": \"CustomerReference\"\n}\n],\n\"AgentAction\": \"\",\n\"ResolutionIntent\": \"\",\n\"SettlementType\": \"\",\n\"singleClearMatch\": false,\n\"Notes\": \"Some text\"\n}\n\nCRITICAL GUARDRAILS\nYou MUST:\n\nPerform deterministic rule evaluation only.\nNever infer or guess programs.\nNever duplicate ProgramId or CustomerTrxId.\nPreserve ProgramName and PromotionCode exactly as provided in input.\nIgnore null or empty claim attributes safely.\nProduce consistent output for identical inputs.\nSource-of-truth restriction:\n\"A Program record can be returned ONLY if ProgramId is present in Program List input. If not, it must not be returned.\"\nNo low-confidence program objects:\n\"Do not output placeholder/zero-confidence programs. If no program meets match criteria, output MatchedPrograms: [].\""
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Run in Parallel"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "0": "1773676795221",
                    "1": "1773676991648",
                    "2": "add_1773221645862_2"
                  },
                  "code": "PARALLEL_1773221645863",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1769161295079",
                  "id": "1773221645862",
                  "inputs": [],
                  "type": "PARALLEL"
                },
                {
