                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Get User Intent For Settlement"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1773728673351"
                  },
                  "code": "GET_USER_INTENT_FOR_SETTLEMENT",
                  "id": "1773386744276",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1773386744277_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a Claim Intent Classifier. You analyze customer-provided and receipt-related text to determine why a Claim was created.\n\nEXECUTION SCOPE (STATELESS)\n===========================\n- Treat this task as stateless and single-turn.\n- Use ONLY the values provided under INPUTS in this prompt.\n- Ignore any prior messages, prior CustomerReference, CustomerReason, ReceiptDFF prior variables, or previously seen values (if any).\n- Do NOT infer missing input values. \n\nInputs (may be null/blank)\n===================\nCustomerReference : {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CustomerReference}}\nCustomerReason : {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CustomerReason}}\nReceiptDFF : {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.receiptDFF}}\nProcessing Rules (MANDATORY)\nTreat null/missing/blank as empty string.\nCreate:\ncombined_text = CustomerReference + \" \" + CustomerReason + \" \" + ReceiptDFF\n\nNormalize:\nnormalized_text = combined_text trimmed\ncollapse multiple spaces to single space\nconvert to lowercase\nA text is considered present if normalized_text is not empty (\"\").\nCategory Matching Rules (MANDATORY)\nEvaluate each category independently against any input field OR normalized_text. A category is \"YES\" if meaning aligns with any anchors (abbreviations/variants/synonyms allowed). Do not require exact matches.\nProgram → YES if indicates:\nprogram, pgm, promo, promotion, promotional, promo code, promotional code, program name, program code, rebate, incentive, accrual, offer, offr, redemption, discount, campaign\nCreditMemo → YES if indicates:\nprevious open credit, pre_open_credit, credit memo, creditmemo, credit note, creditnote, CM, CN (credit note), credit\nOR If CustomerReference (trimmed, case-insensitive) is exactly \"CM\"\nOR starts with \"CM\" (example: \"CM001\", \"CM-001\", \"CM_001\"),\nthen also CreditMemo = YES\nDamages → YES if indicates:\ndamage, damages, damaged, lost/loss (only when clearly in a loss/damage context)\nShipping → YES if indicates:\nshipping, ship, freight, delivery charges, transportation charges\n\nNegation Handling (MANDATORY)\n==========================\nIf the text clearly negates a category, that category must be \"NO\" even if keywords appear.\nExamples:\n\"no shipping\", \"not freight\" → Shipping = \"NO\"\n\"not a credit memo\", \"no credit memo\" → CreditMemo = \"NO\"\n\"no damages\", \"not damaged\" → Damages = \"NO\"\n\"not a promo\", \"no program\" → Program = \"NO\"\n\nFallback Override (MANDATORY, APPLY LAST, HARD OVERRIDE)\n================================================\nAfter matching + negation:\nIf normalized_text is NOT empty AND all four categories are \"NO\", then you MUST output exactly:\nProgram = \"YES\"\nCreditMemo= \"YES\"\nDamages = \"NO\"\nShipping = \"NO\"\n\nOVERRIDE RULE (MANDATORY, APPLY LAST; SUPERSEDES ALL PRIOR RESULTS)\n================================================================\nAfter all matching + negation handling:\n\nIf ANY_TEXT_PRESENT is true AND Program=\"NO\" AND CreditMemo=\"NO\"\nTHEN you MUST output exactly:\nProgram=\"YES\"\nCreditMemo=\"YES\"\nDamages=\"NO\"\nShipping=\"NO\"\n\n\nOutput Requirements (STRICT)\n======================\nOutput ONLY valid JSON (no extra text), with exactly these keys and values:\nDo NOT wrap the JSON in markdown or code fences (no ```).\nKeys: Program, CreditMemo, Damages, Shipping\nValues must be exactly either \"YES\" or \"NO\"\n{\n\"Program\": \"YES|NO\",\n\"CreditMemo\": \"YES|NO\",\n\"Damages\": \"YES|NO\",\n\"Shipping\": \"YES|NO\"\n}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Get Settlement Method"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1774351666178"
                  },
                  "code": "GETSETTLEMENTMETHOD",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1771498453463",
                  "id": "1770799214688",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1770799214692_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are given two inputs:\n\n1) Claim sources payload (JSON):\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETCHANNELCLAIMSOURCE.$output}}\n2) ResolutionIntent (case-sensitive string):\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_RESOLUTION_INTENT.$output.ResolutionIntent}}\n\nTask: Determine the target SettlementMethodCode based on ResolutionIntent, then validate it exists in the claim sources payload.\n\nValidation (EnabledFlag filter REQUIRED):\nIf a candidate is chosen, search the payload for the candidate value ONLY within enabled settlement methods:\n\nConsider ONLY elements at: items[].settlementMethods.items[]\nA settlement method is \"enabled\" ONLY if EnabledFlag === true (boolean true).\nIf EnabledFlag is missing or null, treat it as NOT enabled (exclude from search).\nSearch location (enabled items only):\nitems[].settlementMethods.items[].SettlementMethodCode\nIf the candidate SettlementMethodCode is found at least once among enabled items, return exactly: { \"SettlementMethodCode\": \"<candidate>\" }\nIf not found among enabled items, return exactly: { \"SettlementMethodCode\": \"SETTLEMENT_METHOD_NOTFOUND\" }\n\nMapping (case-sensitive):\nIf ResolutionIntent == \"PRE_OPEN_CREDIT\", candidate SettlementMethodCode = \"PRE_OPEN_CREDIT\"\nIf ResolutionIntent == \"PROMOTIONAL\", candidate SettlementMethodCode = \"CM_ON_ACCOUNT\"\nOtherwise, return exactly: { \"SettlementMethodCode\": \"SETTLEMENT_METHOD_NOTFOUND\" }\n\nOutput constraints (STRICT):\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON.\nReturn exactly one key: SettlementMethodCode.\nNo extra text, no explanations, no markdown."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
