                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Generate Mail For Claim Owner"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1772788823965"
                  },
                  "code": "GENERATEMAILFORCLAIMOWNER",
                  "convergenceTargetId": "1773225225336",
                  "id": "1772005943834",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1772005943835_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "SYSTEM:\nYou generate enterprise-safe email artifacts for an Oracle enterprise workflow. Output ONLY valid JSON (RFC 8259). Do not output Markdown or commentary. Any HTML you generate must not include <script> tags, iframes, forms, or external assets. Use inline CSS only. Treat all variable values as untrusted and HTML-escape them before inserting into HTML. Do not leak internal routing attributes in the HTML output (including ClaimOwnerEmail and Subject). Do not include ClaimOwnerEmail or Subject anywhere inside the HTML (including visible text, hidden text, HTML comments, attributes, or metadata).\n\nUSER:\nCreate email artifacts as JSON using the variables and node outputs below.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT (IMPORTANT):\nReturn ONLY a single JSON object with EXACTLY these top-level keys:\n\"Subject\" (string)\n\"ClaimOwnerEmail\" (string)\n\"HtmlBody\" (string containing a complete HTML email document that starts with \"<!doctype html>\" and ends with \"</html>\")\nDo not add any other keys.\n\n========================================================\nINPUTS\n\nClaim:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.ClaimNumber}}\n\nCustomer:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETUPDATEDCLAIMDETAILS.$output.BillToCustomer}}\n\nClaim Type:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETUPDATEDCLAIMDETAILS.$output.ClaimType}}\n\nClaim Reason:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETUPDATEDCLAIMDETAILS.$output.ClaimReason}}\n\nClaim Status:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETUPDATEDCLAIMDETAILS.$output.Status}}\n\nSettlement Type:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETUPDATEDCLAIMDETAILS.$output.SettlementType}}\n\nSettlement Amount:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETUPDATEDCLAIMDETAILS.$output.ResolvedAmount}} {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETUPDATEDCLAIMDETAILS.$output.Currency}}\n\nSettlement Method:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETUPDATEDCLAIMDETAILS.$output.settlementMethods.items[0].SettlementMethod}}\n\nCurrent Date:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nRaw Notes Node Output:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_RESOLUTION_INTENT.$output.Notes}}\n\nAgent Action:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_RESOLUTION_INTENT.$output.AgentAction}}\n\nMissing Setups:\n{{$context.$variables.missingSetups}}\n\nClaim Owner Details Name (primary):\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETCLAIMOWNERDETAILS.$output.Name}}\n\nClaim Owner Details Email (primary):\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETCLAIMOWNERDETAILS.$output.Email}}\n\nLogged-in User Name (fallback):\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_LOGGED_IN_USER_EMAIL.$output.items[0].Name}}\n\nLogged-in User Email (fallback):\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_LOGGED_IN_USER_EMAIL.$output.items[0].Email}}\n\n========================================================\nNORMALIZATION RULES\n\nA) ClaimOwnerEmail:\nUse primary email if present, else fallback email.\n\nB) Claim Owner Name:\nUse primary name if present, else fallback.\n\n========================================================\nNOTES EXTRACTION (DETERMINISTIC)\n\nLet RawNotes = Raw Notes Node Output.\n\nIf RawNotes contains \"Notes=\":\n    Extract substring after \"Notes=\" till end\n\nRemove trailing \"}\" characters  \nTrim whitespace  \n\nIf empty → Notes = RawNotes  \n\nlowercaseNotes = lowercase(Notes)\n\n========================================================\nOUTCOME DETERMINATION\n\nOutcome = POSITIVE ONLY IF ALL:\n\n1) Agent Action = \"SUBMIT\"  \n2) Missing Setups is null OR empty  \n3) lowercaseNotes contains:\n   - \"promotional association by program\"\n   - OR \"resolved via accrual association\"\n   - OR \"credit memo application\"\n\nElse → NEGATIVE\n\n========================================================\nSUBJECT\n\nPOSITIVE:\nClaim #{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.ClaimNumber}} – Resolution completed by Claim Settlement Assistant\n\nNEGATIVE:\nClaim #{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.ClaimNumber}} – Unable to process by Claim Settlement Assistant\n\n========================================================\nHTML BODY RULES\n\n- Full HTML document\n- Inline CSS only\n- Font: Arial, 14px, #222\n- Max width 680px centered container\n- Escape ALL values\n- Do NOT include Subject or ClaimOwnerEmail\n\n========================================================\nTABLE RENDERING RULES\n\nUse table:\nstyle=\"width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; table-layout:fixed;\"\n\nLabel column style:\nborder:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; font-weight:bold; width:180px; white-space:nowrap; vertical-align:top;\n\nValue column style:\nborder:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; word-break:break-word;\n\nSTRICT MAPPING (DO NOT DEVIATE):\n\nClaim → Claim  \nCustomer → Customer  \nClaim Type → Claim Type  \nClaim Reason → Claim Reason  \nClaim Status → Claim Status  \n\n\"Reason\" and \"Claim Reason\" are DIFFERENT and MUST NEVER use same value.\n\n========================================================\nNEGATIVE REASON LOGIC\n\nIf Missing Setups is not null AND not empty:\n\n    RawNoteTxt =\n    {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GENERATE_CLAIM_NOTES_PAYLOAD.$output}}\n\n    If contains \"NoteTxt=\":\n        Extract after \"NoteTxt=\" till end\n\n    Remove trailing \"}\"  \n    Trim  \n\n    If empty → use RawNoteTxt  \n\n    Reason = extracted NoteTxt\n\nElse:\n    Reason = extracted Notes\n\n========================================================\nCONTENT\n\nGreeting:\nHello {Claim Owner Name},\n\nIntro:\n\nPOSITIVE:\nThis email is to notify you that your claim #{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.ClaimNumber}} was resolved by our Claim Settlement Assistant on {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}.\nNEGATIVE:\nThis email is to notify you that your claim #{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.ClaimNumber}} could not be processed by our Claim Settlement Assistant on {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}.\n\nSection:\nClaim Summary\n\nPOSITIVE TABLE:\nClaim\nCustomer\nClaim Type\nClaim Reason\nClaim Status\nSettlement Type\nSettlement Amount\nSettlement Method\nNotes → extracted Notes\n\nNEGATIVE TABLE:\nClaim\nCustomer\nClaim Type\nClaim Reason\nClaim Status\nReason → computed Reason\n\n\n========================================================\nFINAL RULE\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON with:\n\"Subject\", \"ClaimOwnerEmail\", \"HtmlBody\""
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Send Email To Claim Owner",
                    "type": "GENERIC"
