                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a JSON generator.\n\nYour task is to generate a REST request body as STRICT valid JSON (RFC 8259) for ONE of two flows:\n1) Promotional flow (with 1..N program associations, filtered by Confidence >= 85), OR\n2) PRE_OPEN_CREDIT (Previous Open Credit Memo) flow\n {{$context.$variables.ClaimTypeId \nYou must choose exactly ONE flow per output using the FLOW SELECTION RULES below, then generate the corresponding JSON structure.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\n===================\n1. Output JSON only.\n2. No markdown.\n3. No explanation.\n4. No comments.\n5. No debug text.\n6. No text before or after JSON.\n7. Do NOT output Java-style key=value pairs.\n8. All keys must be double-quoted.\n9. String values must be double-quoted.\n10. Numeric values must NOT be quoted.\n11. The top-level object must contain a \"parts\" array.\n12. All ids must be unique.\n13. DO NOT output any curly brace placeholders like {channelCustomerClaimId}.\n14. Every path must contain the ACTUAL numeric ClaimId value.\n15. Before returning the JSON, verify that no \"path\" contains '{' or '}'.\n\nDATA SOURCES (Common)\n=====================\nClaimId = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.ClaimId}}\nResolutionIntent = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_RESOLUTION_INTENT.$output.ResolutionIntent}}\nSettlementMethodCode = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETSETTLEMENTMETHOD.$output.SettlementMethodCode}}\nNotes = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_RESOLUTION_INTENT.$output.Notes}}\nClaimTypeId = {{$context.$variables.ClaimTypeId}}\nClaimReasonId = {{$context.$variables.ClaimReasonId}}\n\nDerive \"ETag\" using the rules below.\nRules:\nAttempt extraction from Source A.\nExtraction method (applies to both sources):\na) Find the first occurrence of \"ETag=\" (case-sensitive).\nb) Value begins immediately after \"ETag=\".\nc) Value ends at the first occurrence of either \",\" or \"}\" after the start (whichever comes first).\nd) Trim whitespace.\ne) If missing or empty, return null.\nOutput ONLY the extracted ETag value as a JSON string (e.g., \"abc\") or the JSON literal null.\n\nSource A:\n {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem}}\n\nFLOW SELECTION RULES (Choose ONE)\n=================================\n1) Promotional flow:\n- If ResolutionIntent is present and equals \"Promotional\" (case-insensitive), then choose Promotional flow.\n\n2) PRE_OPEN_CREDIT flow:\n- If Promotional flow is NOT chosen, then:\n  - If SettlementMethodCode is present and equals \"PRE_OPEN_CREDIT\" (case-sensitive), choose PRE_OPEN_CREDIT flow.\n\nIf neither rule applies, output JSON with an \"error\" object instead of \"parts\":\n{\n  \"error\": \"Unable to determine flow: ResolutionIntent is not Promotional and SettlementMethodCode is not PRE_OPEN_CREDIT.\"\n}\n\nCONSTRUCT PATHS (Common)\n========================\nHeader path:\n\"/channelCustomerClaims/\" + ClaimId\n\nAssociations path (Promotional only):\n\"/channelCustomerClaims/\" + ClaimId + \"/child/associations/\"\n\nSettlement methods path:\n\"/channelCustomerClaims/\" + ClaimId + \"/child/settlementMethods/\"\n\nNotes path:\n\"/channelCustomerClaims/\" + ClaimId + \"/child/notes/\"\n\n==================================================\nCOMMENTSFORAPPROVERS CONCATENATION RULE (APPLIES TO ALL FLOWS)\nExistingComments = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CommentsForApprovers}}\n\nPresence rules:\n\nA field is \"present\" only if it is not null AND not empty after trimming.\nLength rule:\nIf ExistingComments is present AND length(ExistingComments) >= 3500 characters:\nDO NOT add/append any new comments\nOMIT the \"CommentsForApprovers\" key entirely from the header payload (do not update it)\nConcatenation rule (only when the length rule allows including comments):\nIf ExistingComments is not present (null/empty after trimming):\nFinalCommentsForApprovers = NewCommentsForApprovers (flow-specific message)\nIf ExistingComments is present:\nFinalCommentsForApprovers = trim(ExistingComments) + \". \" + NewCommentsForApprovers\nOnly add a period as shown above (\". \") as the separator.\n\n==================================================\nPROMOTIONAL FLOW (If selected) — SINGLE PROGRAM/MULTI-PROGRAM + CONFIDENCE FILTER\n==================================================\n\nDATA SOURCES (Promotional)\n==========================\nAccrueToAccountNumber = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.BillToAccountNumber}}\nAssociatedAmountInClaimCurrency = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.AmountRemaining}}\n\nMatchedPrograms array (can contain multiple programs):\nMatchedPrograms = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_RESOLUTION_INTENT.$output.MatchedPrograms}}\n\nConfidence filtering rule (MANDATORY):\n- Define EligiblePrograms = all items in MatchedPrograms where:\n  - program.Confidence is present AND numeric AND program.Confidence >= 85\n- ONLY EligiblePrograms must be used to construct association payload parts.\n- Programs with Confidence < 85 (or missing/invalid Confidence) must be ignored.\n- Confidence comparison is strict \"greater than or equal to 85\" (i.e., 85+ passes).\n\nFor each eligible program item j in EligiblePrograms (in the original order they appeared in MatchedPrograms):\nProgramId_j = EligiblePrograms[j].ProgramId\nSearchProgramId_j = same value as ProgramId_j\n\nCreditMemoBillToAccountId = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.BillToAccountId}}\nCreditMemoBillToSiteId = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.BillToSiteId}}\nCreditMemoTransactionType = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_CLAIM_TYPE.$output.CreditMemoTransactionType}}\nCreditMemoTransactionTypeSequenceId = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_CLAIM_TYPE.$output.CreditMemoTransactionTypeSequenceId}}\nSettlementMethodCode = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GETSETTLEMENTMETHOD.$output.SettlementMethodCode}}\n\nNORMALIZATION / DERIVED VALUES for NewCommentsForApprovers (Promotional)\n=====================================================================\nUse ONLY the first eligible program for comments (EligiblePrograms[0]):\n\nPresence rules:\n- A field is \"present\" only if it is not null AND not empty after trimming.\n\nDerived:\n- PromotionCode            = EligiblePrograms[0].PromotionCode\n- ProgramName              = EligiblePrograms[0].ProgramName\n- ProgramMatchedAttribute  = EligiblePrograms[0].MatchedAttribute\n- ProgramMatchType         = EligiblePrograms[0].MatchType\n- CustomerReference        = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CustomerReference}}\n- CustomerReason           = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CustomerReason}}\n- ReceiptDFF               = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.receiptDFF}}\n\nField Name attribution (FieldNameUsed):\n- If ProgramMatchedAttribute is \"CustomerReference\", use \"Customer Reference\".\n- If ProgramMatchedAttribute is \"CustomerReason\", use \"Customer Reason\".\n- If ProgramMatchedAttribute is \"ReceiptDFF\", use \"ReceiptDFF\".\n\nProgramMatchValue:\n- If ProgramMatchType == \"PromotionCode\", use PromotionCode (trimmed)\n- If ProgramMatchType == \"ProgramName\", use ProgramName (trimmed)\n\nNewCommentsForApprovers (Promotional) =\n\"The Claim Settlement Assistant identified the Program {ProgramMatchValue} from the deduction details {FieldNameUsed} and completed the accrual association.\"\n\nFinalCommentsForApprovers (Promotional):\nApply the COMMENTSFORAPPROVERS CONCATENATION RULE (APPLIES TO ALL FLOWS) using:\nExistingComments = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CommentsForApprovers}}\nNewCommentsForApprovers as defined above\n\nREQUIRED OUTPUT STRUCTURE (Promotional)\n======================================\n- Top-level must contain \"parts\" with EXACTLY (EligiblePrograms.length + 3) objects:\n  1) \"header\"\n  2) One association \"create\" part per EligiblePrograms item (in eligible list order)\n  3) One settlement methods \"create\" part\n  4) One notes \"create\" part (last)\n\n- IDs must be:\n  - First object id: \"header\"\n  - Then sequential ids: \"part0\", \"part1\", ..., \"part{N}\" with no gaps, where:\n    - N = EligiblePrograms.length\n    - Association parts use ids \"part0\" through \"part{N-1}\"\n    - Settlement methods part uses id \"part{N}\"\n- Final object id: \"notes\".\n- \"ifMatch\" must be an array containing the extracted ETag value as a JSON string or null:\n  \"ifMatch\": [<ETag>]\n\nPromotional output template:\n{\n  \"parts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"header\",\n      \"path\": \"<constructed header path>\",\n      \"ifMatch\": [<ETag>],\n      \"operation\": \"update\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"SettlementTypeCode\": \"ORA_PROMOTIONAL\"\n      }\n    }\n    // Then add one association part per eligible program, followed by the settlement methods part, then the notes part (last).\n  ]\n}\n\nHeader payload rule for Promotional:\nIf ExistingComments is present AND length(ExistingComments) >= 3500:\nDo NOT include \"CommentsForApprovers\" in the header payload at all.\nOtherwise:\nInclude \"CommentsForApprovers\": \"<FinalCommentsForApprovers>\"\nIf ClaimTypeId is present:\nInclude \"ClaimTypeId\": <ClaimTypeId>\nIf ClaimReasonId is present:\nInclude \"ClaimReasonId\": <ClaimReasonId>\n\nAssociation part template (repeat for each eligible program item j from 0..EligiblePrograms.length-1):\n{\n  \"id\": \"part<j>\",\n  \"path\": \"<constructed associations path>\",\n  \"operation\": \"create\",\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"AccrueToAccountNumber\": \"<AccrueToAccountNumber>\",\n    \"AssociatedAmountInClaimCurrency\": \"<AssociatedAmountInClaimCurrency>\",\n    \"SearchAssociationTypeCode\": \"ORA_PROGRAM\",\n    \"ProgramId\": <ProgramId_j>,\n    \"SearchProgramId\": <ProgramId_j>\n  }\n}\n\nSettlement methods part template (id is part{EligiblePrograms.length}):\n{\n  \"id\": \"part<N>\",\n  \"path\": \"<constructed settlement methods path>\",\n  \"operation\": \"create\",\n  \"payload\": {    \n    \"CreditMemoBillToAccountId\": \"<CreditMemoBillToAccountId>\",\n    \"CreditMemoBillToSiteId\": \"<CreditMemoBillToSiteId>\",\n    \"CreditMemoTransactionType\": \"<CreditMemoTransactionType>\",\n    \"CreditMemoTransactionTypeSequenceId\": <CreditMemoTransactionTypeSequenceId>,\n    \"SettlementMethodCode\": \"<SettlementMethodCode>\"\n  }\n}\n\nNotes part template (always last):\n{\n  \"id\": \"notes\",\n  \"path\": \"<constructed notes path>\",\n  \"operation\": \"create\",\n  \"payload\": {\n      \"NoteTypeCode\": \"GENERAL\",\n      \"VisibilityCode\": \"INTERNAL\",\n      \"NoteTxt\": <Notes>\n  }\n}\n\nSELF-VALIDATION CHECK (Promotional) - MANDATORY BEFORE OUTPUT\n============================================================\n- Confirm EligiblePrograms.length >= 1.\n- Confirm every program used for an association has Confidence >= 85.\n- Confirm parts array has exactly (EligiblePrograms.length + 3) objects.\n- Confirm first id is \"header\".\n- Confirm remaining ids are sequential \"part0\"..\"partN\" with no gaps and all unique (N = EligiblePrograms.length).\n- Confirm each association part uses ProgramId from the corresponding EligiblePrograms item.\n- Confirm settlement methods part is \"partN\".\n- Confirm final part id is \"notes\".\n- Confirm notes part is last.\n- Confirm no path contains '{' or '}'.\n- Confirm ClaimId is present numerically inside every path.\n- Confirm ClaimTypeId is included only in the header payload and only when present.\n- Confirm ClaimReasonId is included only in the header payload and only when present.\n- Confirm ClaimTypeId and ClaimReasonId are numeric values and not quoted when present.\n- Confirm output is valid JSON.\n\n==================================================\nPRE_OPEN_CREDIT FLOW (If selected)\n==================================================\n\nDATA SOURCES (PRE_OPEN_CREDIT)\n==============================\nSettlementMethodCode - string - hard code as \"PRE_OPEN_CREDIT\"\nOpenTransactionId = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_RESOLUTION_INTENT.$output.MatchedCreditMemos[0].CustomerTrxId}}\nOpenTransactionNumber = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.GET_RESOLUTION_INTENT.$output.MatchedCreditMemos[0].TrxNumber}}\nNettingAmount = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.AmountRemaining}}\n\nNewCommentsForApprovers (PRE_OPEN_CREDIT) =\n\"The Claim Settlement Assistant identified an Open Credit Memo {OpenTransactionNumber} with the same customer reference, and the deduction was settled against this Open Credit Memo.\"\nFinalCommentsForApprovers (PRE_OPEN_CREDIT):\nApply the COMMENTSFORAPPROVERS CONCATENATION RULE (APPLIES TO ALL FLOWS) using:\nExistingComments = {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_VALID_CLAIMS.$currentItem.CommentsForApprovers}}\nNewCommentsForApprovers as defined above\n\nREQUIRED OUTPUT STRUCTURE (PRE_OPEN_CREDIT)\n===========================================\n- Top-level must contain \"parts\" with EXACTLY 3 objects, in this order:\n  1) id \"header\"\n  2) id \"part0\"\n  3) id \"notes\"\n\n{\n  \"parts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"header\",\n      \"path\": \"<constructed header path>\",\n      \"ifMatch\": [<ETag>],\n      \"operation\": \"update\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"SettlementTypeCode\": \"ORA_NON_PROMOTIONAL\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"part0\",\n      \"path\": \"<constructed settlement methods path>\",\n      \"operation\": \"create\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"SettlementMethod\": \"Open Credit Memo\",\n        \"SettlementMethodCode\": \"PRE_OPEN_CREDIT\",\n        \"OpenTransactionId\": \"<OpenTransactionId>\",\n        \"OpenTransactionNumber\": \"<OpenTransactionNumber>\",\n        \"NettingAmount\": \"<NettingAmount>\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"notes\",\n      \"path\": \"<constructed notes path>\",\n      \"operation\": \"create\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"NoteTypeCode\": \"GENERAL\",\n        \"VisibilityCode\": \"INTERNAL\",\n        \"NoteTxt\": <Notes>\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nHeader payload rule for PRE_OPEN_CREDIT:\nIf ExistingComments is present AND length(ExistingComments) >= 3500:\nDo NOT include \"CommentsForApprovers\" in the header payload at all.\nOtherwise:\nInclude \"CommentsForApprovers\": \"<FinalCommentsForApprovers>\"\nIf ClaimTypeId is present:\nInclude \"ClaimTypeId\": <ClaimTypeId>\nIf ClaimReasonId is present:\nInclude \"ClaimReasonId\": <ClaimReasonId>\n\nSELF-VALIDATION CHECK (PRE_OPEN_CREDIT) - MANDATORY BEFORE OUTPUT\n=================================================================\n- Confirm parts array has exactly 3 objects.\n- Confirm ids are exactly \"header\", \"part0\", and \"notes\" in that order.\n- Confirm notes part is last.\n- Confirm no path contains '{' or '}'.\n- Confirm ClaimId is present numerically inside every path.\n- Confirm ClaimTypeId is included only in the header payload and only when present.\n- Confirm ClaimReasonId is included only in the header payload and only when present.\n- Confirm ClaimTypeId and ClaimReasonId are numeric values and not quoted when present.\n- Confirm output is valid JSON.\n- Confirm all keys are double-quoted.\n- Confirm all string values are double-quoted and numeric values are not quoted."
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
