                  },
                  "code": "CREATE_NOTES_PAYLOAD_FOR_INVALID_CLAIMS",
                  "id": "1773740365131",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1773740365131_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "You are a deterministic **Claim Settlement Assistant – Internal Note Generator**.\n\nTASK\nUsing the inputs below, select the correct scenario (by precedence rules) and produce ONE output JSON object in the exact “OUTPUT JSON SHAPE” format. The JSON must include the computed note text in NoteTxt.\n\nIMPORTANT OUTPUT CONSTRAINTS\n- Output ONLY the JSON object (no markdown, no commentary, no extra keys).\n- The JSON must match the exact structure and key names in OUTPUT JSON SHAPE.\n- Replace <ClaimId> in the path with the ClaimId value.\n\n========================================================\nINPUTS (treat these expressions as the values to use)\n========================================================\nClaimId                 : {{$context.$nodes.LOOP_INVALID_CLAIMS_ARRAY.$currentItem.ClaimId}} \n\n========================================================\nOUTPUT JSON SHAPE (MUST MATCH EXACTLY)\n========================================================\n\n{\n  \"parts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"part0\",\n      \"path\": \"/channelCustomerClaims/<ClaimId>/child/notes/\",\n      \"operation\": \"create\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"NoteTypeCode\": \"GENERAL\",\n        \"VisibilityCode\": \"INTERNAL\",\n        \"NoteTxt\": \"The Claim Settlement Assistant identified that the settlement details were already updated by the user in this claim. To avoid overriding user updates, the agent skipped the automated settlement. This note is provided for reference based on the agent’s evaluation.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Generate Mail For Claim Owner For Invalid Claims"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
                    "success": "1776442115277"
                  },
                  "code": "GENERATE_MAIL_FOR_CLAIM_OWNER_FOR_INVALID_CLAIMS",
                  "id": "1776441912421",
                  "inputs": [
                    {
                      "id": "1776441912425_1",
                      "name": "prompt",
                      "type": "string",
                      "value": "SYSTEM:\nYou generate enterprise-safe email artifacts for an Oracle enterprise workflow. Output ONLY valid JSON (RFC 8259). Do not output Markdown or commentary. Any HTML you generate must not include <script> tags, iframes, forms, or external assets. Use inline CSS only. Treat all variable values as untrusted and HTML-escape them before inserting into HTML. Do not leak internal routing attributes in the HTML output (including ClaimOwnerEmail and Subject). Do not include ClaimOwnerEmail or Subject anywhere inside the HTML (including visible text, hidden text, HTML comments, attributes, or metadata).\n\nUSER:\nCreate email artifacts as JSON using the variables and node outputs below.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENT (IMPORTANT):\nReturn ONLY a single JSON object with EXACTLY these top-level keys:\n\"Subject\" (string)\n\"ClaimOwnerEmail\" (string)\n\"HtmlBody\" (string containing a complete HTML email document that starts with \"<!doctype html>\" and ends with \"</html>\")\nDo not add any other keys.\n\n========================================================\nINPUTS\n\nClaim:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_INVALID_CLAIMS_ARRAY.$currentItem.ClaimNumber}}\n\nCustomer:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_INVALID_CLAIMS_ARRAY.$currentItem.BillToCustomer}}\n\nClaim Type:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_INVALID_CLAIMS_ARRAY.$currentItem.ClaimType}}\n\nClaim Reason:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_INVALID_CLAIMS_ARRAY.$currentItem.ClaimReason}}\n\nClaim Status:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_INVALID_CLAIMS_ARRAY.$currentItem.Status}}\n\nCurrent Date:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\n\nReason: \n\"The Claim Settlement Assistant identified that the settlement details were already updated by the user in this claim. To avoid overriding user updates, the agent skipped the automated settlement. This note is provided for reference based on the agent’s evaluation.\"\n\nClaim Owner Details Name (primary):\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_INVALID_CLAIMS_ARRAY.GET_OWNER_DETAIL.$output.Name}}\n\nClaim Owner Details Email (primary):\n{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_INVALID_CLAIMS_ARRAY.GET_OWNER_DETAIL.$output.Email}}\n\nLogged-in User Name (fallback):\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_LOGGED_IN_USER_EMAIL.$output.items[0].Name}}\n\nLogged-in User Email (fallback):\n{{$context.$nodes.GET_LOGGED_IN_USER_EMAIL.$output.items[0].Email}}\n\n========================================================\nNORMALIZATION RULES\n\nA) ClaimOwnerEmail:\nUse primary email if present, else fallback email.\n\nB) Claim Owner Name:\nUse primary name if present, else fallback.\n\n========================================================\nSUBJECT\n\nClaim #{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_INVALID_CLAIMS_ARRAY.$currentItem.ClaimNumber}} – Unable to process by Claim Settlement Assistant\n\n========================================================\nHTML BODY RULES\n\n- Full HTML document\n- Inline CSS only\n- Font: Arial, 14px, #222\n- Max width 680px centered container\n- Escape ALL values\n- Do NOT include Subject or ClaimOwnerEmail\n\n========================================================\nTABLE RENDERING RULES\n\nUse table:\nstyle=\"width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; table-layout:fixed;\"\n\nLabel column style:\nborder:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; font-weight:bold; width:180px; white-space:nowrap; vertical-align:top;\n\nValue column style:\nborder:1px solid #ccc; padding:8px; vertical-align:top; word-break:break-word;\n\nSTRICT MAPPING (DO NOT DEVIATE):\n\nClaim → Claim  \nCustomer → Customer  \nClaim Type → Claim Type  \nClaim Reason → Claim Reason  \nClaim Status → Claim Status\n\nCONTENT\n\nGreeting:\nHello {Claim Owner Name},\n\nIntro:\n\nThis email is to notify you that your claim #{{$context.$nodes.LOOP_INVALID_CLAIMS_ARRAY.$currentItem.ClaimNumber}} could not be processed by our Claim Settlement Assistant on {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}.\n\nSection:\nClaim Summary\n\nTABLE:\nClaim\nCustomer\nClaim Type\nClaim Reason\nClaim Status\nReason\n\n========================================================\nFINAL RULE\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON with:\n\"Subject\", \"ClaimOwnerEmail\", \"HtmlBody\""
                    }
                  ],
                  "type": "LLM"
                },
                {
                  "metadata": {
                    "name": "Send Email To Claim Owner For Invalid Claims",
                    "type": "GENERIC"
                  },
                  "outcomes": {
